WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:05.296
Question three: can the solution clean or delete the issue?

2
00:00:05.296 --> 00:00:12.849
And to finish, I run the whole status check on one workstation with PowerShell, WKS-TRN-07,

3
00:00:12.849 --> 00:00:17.247
exactly as you will on your own seat in Activity 7.4.

4
00:00:18.347 --> 00:00:19.817
Is it installed?

5
00:00:19.817 --> 00:00:22.664
Get-Service lists the services.

6
00:00:22.664 --> 00:00:27.808
CSFalconService, the CrowdStrike EDR sensor, is running.

7
00:00:27.808 --> 00:00:29.645
WazuhSvc is running.

8
00:00:29.645 --> 00:00:33.502
WinDefend, Microsoft Defender, is running.

9
00:00:33.502 --> 00:00:37.451
All three required solutions are installed.

10
00:00:38.551 --> 00:00:40.303
Is Defender operational?

11
00:00:40.303 --> 00:00:47.311
Real-time protection true, tamper protection true, and the signatures were updated this morning.

12
00:00:48.411 --> 00:00:55.784
A running service does not prove the Wazuh agent is talking to the SIEM, so I read the last lines of its log.

13
00:00:55.784 --> 00:01:00.315
Keep alive acknowledged by manager at nine thirty: it is connected.

14
00:01:01.415 --> 00:01:03.019
Now question three.

15
00:01:03.019 --> 00:01:08.757
Get-MpPreference shows what Defender will do when it finds a threat.

16
00:01:08.757 --> 00:01:11.880
Severe threats: action three, remove.

17
00:01:11.880 --> 00:01:15.931
But high threats: action six, which means allow.

18
00:01:15.931 --> 00:01:20.825
A trojan rated High would be detected and then left alone.

19
00:01:20.825 --> 00:01:22.935
Defender cannot clean it.

20
00:01:22.935 --> 00:01:24.792
No folder is excluded.

21
00:01:25.891 --> 00:01:29.171
Here is the status check for WKS-TRN-07.

22
00:01:29.171 --> 00:01:35.649
Everything is installed and operational, but the clean-up policy fails rule C1.

23
00:01:35.649 --> 00:01:38.109
I report it to the Shift Lead.

24
00:01:38.109 --> 00:01:40.896
I do not change the policy myself.

25
00:01:40.896 --> 00:01:50.736
Remember the other two reasons a solution cannot clean: an exclusion on the threat's folder, or EDR in detect-only mode.

26
00:01:50.736 --> 00:01:54.835
And ransomware or a rootkit always means re-image.

27
00:01:55.935 --> 00:01:56.783
Your turn.

28
00:01:56.783 --> 00:01:59.918
In the CTM Virtual Lab, choose Day 7.

29
00:01:59.918 --> 00:02:08.899
In Activity 7.3, decide for eight detections whether the solution can clean them, from each host's policy.

30
00:02:08.899 --> 00:02:14.830
Then in Activity 7.4, run these four commands on your own workstation.

31
00:02:14.830 --> 00:02:16.863
Every seat is different.

